{"id":"cc607be4-379a-4de8-83b2-91587d7228d3","object":"chat.completion","created":1785012709,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate case structure\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must contain 'threshold' and 'calls'\\\")\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        required = ['call_id', 'loss_without_call', 'loss_with_call', 'prediction_tokens', 'parseable']\\n        for key in required:\\n            if key not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"missing field {key} in call\\\")\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be a bool\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) based on the description. The task is \"AGENT-TF-01\" which is about filtering API calls based on a threshold and normalized gain. The case payload has \"threshold\" and \"calls\" list. Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable.\n\nWe need to compute for each call: gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Normalized gain = gain / prediction_tokens. (Assuming at least one token, but if prediction_tokens could be 0? The description says \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" So if prediction_tokens is 0? In fixtures they are >0. But to be safe, we could handle zero? But likely not needed. We'll assume positive integer.)\n\nThen the call is accepted if parseable is True AND normalized_gain >= threshold. (Inclusive threshold.)\n\nWe need to output accepted_call_ids (list of accepted call_ids in original order) and diagnostics array, each with accepted (boolean), call_id, normalized_gain (rounded?). The description says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" Also the output schema says normalized_gain is number, but likely needs to be rounded to some precision? Not specified. The diagnostics should be in supplied call order. We'll compute normalized_gain to a reasonable precision, maybe keep as float? The fixture outputs? Not given. But we can round to, say, 6 decimal places? Or just keep as is? Since it's a number, JSON supports floats. The task says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify precision. In examples? Not provided. We'll assume we round to, say, 6 decimal places using round(x, 6) or maybe just use the exact float. But to be safe, we can keep as is. However, the schema says type number, so any float is fine. But to avoid floating point issues, we could round to a reasonable number of decimals. I'll use round(x, 6) or maybe keep as is. Let's see the description: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" Possibly they want rounding to some precision, but not specified. In many tasks, they use round(x, 5) or similar. Since it's not specified, I'll assume we can output the computed normalized_gain as a Python float (which is double). The output contract doesn't impose rounding. I'll just compute normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (float division). Then we need to return diagnostics array with each call in order.\n\nAccepted_call_ids should be list of call_ids for which accepted is True.\n\nWe must not mutate case.\n\nWe must raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. So we should validate fields.\n\nWe need to implement solve(case) and return dict with keys \"accepted_call_ids\" and \"diagnostics\".\n\nThe implementation must be in Python standard library only.\n\nWe'll write solve function that takes case (a dict) and returns dict.\n\nWe'll check that case has \"threshold\" and \"calls\". Calls list must be present and each call must have required fields.\n\nWe'll iterate over calls, compute normalized_gain, check parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold, then build diagnostics and accepted list.\n\nReturn JSON-serializable output.\n\nNow, we need to produce the answer as JSON with single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source code as a JSON-escaped string.\n\nWe'll write the source code with proper indentation.\n\nNote: The function signature is solve(case). We'll define it accordingly.\n\nLet's craft the implementation."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason